- op: create  # cafd
  at: '2026-10-01T09:04:51Z'  # cafd
  by: agent  # cafd
  actor: jgstern_agent  # cafd
  clock: 1  # cafd
  nonce: cafd  # cafd
  data:  # cafd
    kind: work_item  # cafd
    title: "go: a selector-form function reference (register(pkg.Handler), Command{RunE: pkg.Run}) is resolved by its field name repo-wide -- reg(http.NotFound) binds a repo function NotFound at 0.70"  # cafd
    status: todo_hard  # cafd
    priority: 3  # cafd
    parent:  # cafd
    tags:  # cafd
    - go  # cafd
    - call_graph  # cafd
    - analysis_quality  # cafd
    isbefore: []  # cafd
    duplicate_of: []  # cafd
    not_duplicate_of: []  # cafd
    pr_ref:  # cafd
    description: "FOUND 2026-10-01 while fixing WI-bivin-ronup-kuzam-giliz-sinoz-gihug-tigas-rovom (branch jgstern-agent/fix/bivin, not merged).\n\ngo.py resolves the SELECTOR form of a function reference by its field name alone, repo-wide, with no package or receiver evidence: in _extract_function_reference_edges (a function passed as an argument, r.Get(\"/x\", h.GetAPI) or register(pkg.Handler)) and in the keyed_element arm (cobra.Command{RunE: pkg.Run}), both call resolver.lookup(ref_name) with no path_hint. The operand is never consulted: an import alias (pkg.Handler) is not turned into the import-path hint the call arm uses, and a typed receiver (h.GetAPI with h of a known type) is not turned into Type.GetAPI. So:\n- a name declared once anywhere in the repo binds there at 0.70, even when the operand is an EXTERNAL package (http.NotFound -> a repo function NotFound);\n- two candidates bind the path-sorted first at 0.70/sqrt(2) = 0.49;\n- three or more bind nothing (ambiguity_threshold=3).\n\nWI-bivin fixed the BARE-identifier form of both arms (caller's own package only). The selector form is the same missing-evidence mechanism on a different construct and was deliberately left out of that branch.\n\nLive repro (analyze_go on the bivin branch; package a declares func NotFound(), package b does reg(http.NotFound) and C{H: http.NotFound} with \"net/http\" imported): Use -> a/a.go NotFound twice, function_reference_arg 0.70 and struct_field_reference 0.70 -- a call edge into a package b never imports, for a stdlib function.\n\nNOT MEASURED: frequency on the corpus; how many selector refs have an import-alias operand vs a typed-receiver operand vs an untyped one. Related: WI-ravav-ruguz-loziz-kajag-milub-naval-bufar-dadil (whether a struct-literal field value should be a calls edge at all).\n\nACCEPTANCE: a selector function reference whose operand is an import alias resolves only within the imported package (or to the unresolved placeholder for an external package); one whose operand has a tracked type resolves to Type.method; neither falls back to a repo-wide short-name pick."  # cafd
    fields: {}  # cafd
- op: discuss  # 2bb4
  at: '2026-10-03T06:42:04Z'  # 2bb4
  by: agent  # 2bb4
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 2bb4
  clock: 2  # 2bb4
  nonce: 2bb4  # 2bb4
  message: "PREMISE AUDIT 2026-10-03 (owner-requested; read-only, reproduced at dev 3abedae588 on small fixtures). PARTLY STALE: premise holds; branch context outdated.\n- go.py:3245-3277 (_extract_function_reference_edges, selector arm) calls resolver.lookup(ref_name) with no path_hint and never consults the operand; the keyed_element arm (go.py:4386-4400) does the same; the docstring at go.py:3231-3232 says so.\n- Repro: package a declares func NotFound(); package b imports net/http and calls reg(http.NotFound) and C{H: http.NotFound}. Result: Use -> a/NotFound 0.7 function_reference_arg, Use3 -> a/NotFound 0.7 struct_field_reference.\n- OUTDATED: WI-bivin is not \"on the bivin branch, not merged\"; it merged as cbb41dbdbb (PR #1383, 2026-10-01) and is done. The repro above is at HEAD, after it.\n- Related, not a duplicate: WI-ravav (whether a struct-field value should be a calls edge at all)."  # 2bb4
- op: discuss  # 02b4
  at: '2026-10-04T01:25:47Z'  # 02b4
  by: agent  # 02b4
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 02b4
  clock: 3  # 02b4
  nonce: 02b4  # 02b4
  message: "WORK DONE on branch jgstern-agent/fix/kibah (not merged), commit 3fb8b84d20.\n\nA selector in value position (argument arm and struct-field arm) is resolved by its OPERAND (_go_selector_reference_target): an import alias with no local in scope -> a function of that package only, nothing for an outside package (the read stays a module_attr_ref); a typed operand or a composite literal `(&T{}).M` -> that type's method; a method expression `T.M` / `(*T).M` -> that method; anything else -> nothing. No repo-wide short-name pick remains. Live, the filed repro (package a: func NotFound(); package b: reg(http.NotFound), C{H: http.NotFound}): dev -> a/NotFound 0.70 twice; branch -> no calls edge, module_attr_ref net/http.NotFound kept. `reg(a.NotFound)` / `C{H: c.NotFound}` with NotFound in both a and c bind each its own package.\n\nTwo call-arm lookups of the same mechanism, fixed in the same commit: (1) _go_in_hinted_package: ListNameResolver falls back to the path-sorted first of ALL candidates when a hard hint matches none of 2+, so `http.Get(u)` bound a repo Get and alertmanager's `require.Equal` bound InhibitRule.Equal (a FIELD); refused now (sites: alertmanager 403, coredns 53, cert-manager 49, prometheus 150). (2) _go_method_of_type: Type.Method is keyed with an unqualified type, so prometheus' consul test bound eureka's SDConfig.UnmarshalYAML; now taken in the type's package, with one level of struct embedding (moved: 50 / 19 / 155 / 470 sites; to unresolved: 33 / 0 / 21 / 63, residual WI-punat-pivij-laduj-tulot-fumup-hovos-zajan-jokud). Also `var a = &T{}` is now typed like `a := &T{}`.\n\nSelector references removed / added by site: alertmanager -41/+7, coredns -65/+39, cert-manager -124/+46, prometheus -58/+170. Removed sampled: mostly field reads bound to same-named methods/functions (resp.Body, tc.retry, route.Formats, s.TTL); a few correct-by-luck binds through untyped operands are lost. Added: typed method values (prometheus router.Get(\"/version\", h.version)).\n\nTargeted smart-test on HEAD 5e60e3ea7d: 15728 passed, 5 xfailed, 100% coverage on changed files."  # 02b4
- op: discuss  # 2c2c
  at: '2026-10-04T01:41:14Z'  # 2c2c
  by: agent  # 2c2c
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 2c2c
  clock: 4  # 2c2c
  nonce: 2c2c  # 2c2c
  message: "INTEGRATION NOTE from WI-vinuh / WI-nulig (branch jgstern-agent/fix/vinuh, commit 8da3b291eb, not pushed). That branch edits go.py's call arm in _extract_edges_from_file, which a go name-resolution branch is likely to touch too:\n- the arm's entry is now `node.type == \"call_expression\" or (type_conversion_expression and _go_instantiated_callee(...))`; func_node may be a type_identifier / qualified_type, so every `func_node.type == \"identifier\"` / `\"selector_expression\"` test in the arm became `callee_shape == ...`, and the selector branch reads `_go_selector_parts(func_node)` (accepting a package_identifier operand);\n- a new pre-check after the bound-names guard drops an instantiated callee that resolves to a non-function/type;\n- the chained-call branch gained a result-typing arm, and a `receiver_type_is_external` flag (set by the chained, package-variable and field-chain branches) replaces the final resolver lookup with an empty LookupResult;\n- `args_node` for a conversion-spelled call is the node itself, so _extract_function_reference_edges sees its operand (that function itself is unchanged).\nA rebase over a branch that also edits these lines needs the callee_shape rename carried into any new `func_node.type` test."  # 2c2c
